cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the models and datasets it builds on (references)."
title: "Rescue Router: flood maps from 50 labelled drone photos and rescue routes to every house"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Melis
    given-names: Marlen
    affiliation: KAIST
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MarlenMM/rescue-router"
url: "https://marlenmm.github.io/rescue-router/"
keywords:
  - flood mapping
  - few-shot segmentation
  - disaster response
  - routing
  - drone imagery
  - semantic segmentation
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  Flood maps from drone photos (clear road, flooded road, flooded and dry building, water) learned from 50 labelled
  photos, and a truck / boat / on-foot router on 4x4-pixel cells with vehicle widths and confidence tiers, in a static
  web viewer that can also map a photo in the browser. A pre-registered comparison of Chameleon, a few-shot dense
  prediction generalist, with a standard segmenter (DeepLabV3-ResNet50) fine-tuned on the same photos, on FloodNet
  and RescueNet. Research code; not for operational rescue decisions (MODEL_CARD.md).
